Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||12-05-2001||04:54 PM||||I think that associating the Fiero design to that of the similiar era Ferrari is not <I>that</I> far-fetched.  It is quite a coincidence that the 308/328 when compared to the Fiero has many similiarities... wheelbase, engine placement, etc.  NOT that I'm suggesting that GM copied Ferrari, or that the Fiero was designed to compete with them- only that it certainly may have gained some <I>"Inspiration"</I> from them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Even the 308GTO used the "same" displacement 2.8L  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Of course it wasn't quite the same thing... a little difference in power  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-05-2001||10:57 PM||||But they did minn. They bought a Ferrari 308 and played with all the measurements and layout in the initial stages. A lot of critical numbers are very close to each other.||||reg||1
